hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19233","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, he said: Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to me from Fadalah al-Laythi who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and embraced Islam, and he taught me until he taught me the five prayers at their times. I said to him: These are hours in which I am busy, so order me with comprehensive matters. He said to me: If you are busy then do not be busy away from the two Asrs. I said: What are the two Asrs? He said: The dawn prayer and the Asr prayer."
